body:
@zzzeek 
Referring to your [comment](https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/4430#issuecomment-452381434) on issue #4430 asking for PR for this. It's not clear what you envision as a fix here. I think we should find out what was the original idea behind current code. What do you think?

We noticed this problem on Python 2 while using cx_Oracle with `NLS_LANG` set to `polish_poland.AL32UTF8` which results in error messages being utf8 encoded and of type `str`. Arguably they should have been of type `unicode` which I raised as oracle/python-cx_Oracle/issues/253

this is the simplest change:

```
    def _message(self):

        if len(self.args) == 1:
            msg = self.args[0]
        else:
            msg = self.args

        return msg

```

so...why isnt that what it is?   so I need to look in the history because I'm 99% sure that text_type() is there because someone reported a bug about 8 years ago
